<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.6.1: Using Linear Functions to Describe Constant Speed</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01830</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.6.1: Using Linear Functions to Describe Constant Speed</md:title>
    <md:uuid>518e776a-129a-44b3-bc9c-e2e6bbb047fd</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>A cannon is 10 feet off the ground. It launches a cannonball straight up with a velocity of 406 feet per second.</para>
<para>Imagine that there is no gravity and that the cannonball continues to travel upward with the same velocity.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Answer questions a–f using the table with the heights of the cannonball at different times.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Seconds
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Distance above ground (feet)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        10
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        a. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        b. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        c. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
        d. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        5
      </entry>
      <entry>
        e. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(t\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
        f. _____
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="2dddc6ef-d362-494e-916e-671468e34813" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3a577da6-6105-4e46-85c7-cb4e068e4bfe" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="416">
    <problem>
      <para> How far above the ground is the cannonball at 1 second?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cannonball is 416 feet above the ground at 1 second.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6bb155ed-6a1c-4114-9f67-9ad53bae0313" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="822">
    <problem>
      <para> How far above the ground is the cannonball at 2 seconds?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cannonball is 822 feet above the ground at 2 seconds.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="391c299f-b35d-4c3f-b372-744ba36d15f2" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1228">
    <problem>
      <para> How far above the ground is the cannonball at 3 seconds?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cannonball is 1,228 feet above the ground at 3 seconds.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="74878a62-1f11-4e7f-bf75-6d943723008b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1634">
    <problem>
      <para> How far above the ground is the cannonball at 4 seconds?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cannonball is 1634 feet above the ground at 4 seconds.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7676f221-e8dc-4062-b482-97ca000c4044" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2040">
    <problem>
      <para> How far above the ground is the cannonball at 5 seconds?</para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cannonball is 2040 feet above the ground at 5 seconds.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
